Z||000000||CraigH||04-12-2001||01:26 AM||||I just purchased 2 Fieros.  One is a 1984 4cyl with an automatic trans.  The other is a 1985 V6 with a manual trans.  Can I put the automatic trans from the 4 cyl. into the V6?||||reg||1
Z||000001||86GT Turbo||04-12-2001||01:39 AM||||Whats up<P>you can't put a 2.5 auto trans in a V6<BR>because if the internals of the trans <BR>plus you need a wiring harness and ecm out<BR>of a V6 auto<BR>the best thing to do if you want a auto in your V6 is to find some one that has done a swap<BR>I have a auto trans out of a 85 V6<BR>but it needs to be rebuilt<BR>I also have some of the other stuff but not all of it.<P>Turbo||||reg||9
Z||000002||Galen||04-12-2001||01:58 AM||||Pardon my humble opinion, but the 3spd auto tranny used on the v6s is the same as the one used on the i4s.. I know I am not the brightest guy in the world. But this I do know. Howevery, you will need the computer for a auto v6, as well as the wiring harness for the TCC.<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||86GT Turbo||04-12-2001||02:08 AM||||<BR>I have rebuilt about 15 TH125 trans <BR>the main drum and gearing packs are diffrent<BR>TH125 are coded you could probley do it<BR>but with all that trouble why not do it right<P>Turbo||||reg||11
Z||000004||Galen||04-12-2001||02:14 AM||||I dunno, I think I'm gonna stick to my opinion. Ogre could prolly back me up, if he dont. I will admit my wrongness. But I do belive I am correct, I could be wrong but I think I am correct. And as I have said correct too many times now. I will click submit||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||04-12-2001||02:22 AM||||I am not sure if the difference has to do with 4-cyl or V-6 but I know that the Auto's have 2 different gear ratio's. One is 3.08 and the other is 3.65.<BR>I also know that both have been used for V-8 conversions so there is not a reliability issue using the 84 trans on an 85 V-6. But I know you do need an ECM from a V-6 Auto.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||04-12-2001||05:47 AM||||i checked into this last year at TwinCities Fiero. the computer and entire dash wiring harness has to be changed.||||reg||1
